// The payment provider name comes from PAYMENT_PROVIDER in src/lib/site.ts.
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { PAYMENT_PROVIDER } from '../lib/site';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Consultation Terms"
  heading="Advisory Session Terms"
  description="Booking, payment, cancellation and refund terms for paid advisory sessions with Results Matrix Limited."
>
  <p>
    These terms apply to the paid advisory sessions described on our
    <a href="/consultations/">consultations page</a>. They are between you (or the organization you
    book for) and Results Matrix Limited ("RML", "we", "us"). By requesting an invoice or paying
    for a session, you agree to them. Larger or longer engagements are covered by their own written
    agreement, which takes priority over these terms where the two differ.
  </p>

  <h2>What a session includes</h2>
  <p>
    A session is a 60-minute one-to-one advisory call with an RML senior consultant, followed by a
    written recommendations memo and follow-up email support limited to questions about that
    memo. The features listed on the consultations page at the time you book describe what you are
    buying.
  </p>

  <h2>Booking</h2>
  <p>
    Booking is confirmed when we have received payment or, for organizations paying by invoice,
    when we have received your payment or a purchase order we have accepted in writing. After
    that we send you a private scheduling link so you can choose a time. Scheduling links are sent
    to the payer and should not be shared.
  </p>
  <p>
    Please send us any documents we should review at least two working days before the session.
    We can only advise on what we have been given, so the quality of the advice depends on the
    accuracy and completeness of your information.
  </p>

  <h2>Fees and payment</h2>
  <p>
    The fee is shown at the time you book or on your invoice, in the currency stated there. Taxes,
    such as General Consumption Tax, are added where they apply and are shown on the invoice or at
    checkout.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Pay online.</strong> You are sent to the checkout of our payment provider,
      {PAYMENT_PROVIDER}, which processes your payment on its own platform. Your card details are
      entered there and never reach the Site or RML, and the provider's own terms and privacy
      notice apply to that payment.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Bank transfer or invoice.</strong> Request an invoice through the form on the
      consultations page. We issue an invoice with our bank details and a payment reference. Please
      pay by the due date shown on it. Any bank charges on your side are yours to bear, so the
      full invoiced amount reaches us.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Rescheduling and cancellation by you</h2>
  <p>
    You can move your session to another time, once and free of charge, if you tell us at least 48
    hours before it starts. If you cancel with at least 48 hours' notice you are entitled to a
    refund under the refunds section below.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you cancel or ask to reschedule with less than 48 hours' notice, or do not attend, the
    session is treated as delivered and the fee is not refundable. We may, at our discretion,
    offer you a new time as a courtesy. If you are more than 15 minutes late we may end the
    session at its scheduled finish time.
  </p>

  <h2>Cancellation or rescheduling by us</h2>
  <p>
    If we need to cancel or move a session, we will tell you as soon as we can and offer you a new
    time. If no new time works for you, we will refund the fee in full.
  </p>

  <h2>Refunds</h2>
  <p>
    Where a refund is due, we pay it in full to the account or card that made the payment, within
    30 days of agreeing the refund. Once a session has been delivered, fees are not refundable. If
    you are unhappy with a session, tell us within seven days at
    <a href="mailto:info@resultsmatrix.com">info@resultsmatrix.com</a>
    and we will work with you to put it right, which may include a follow-up call or a revised
    memo.
  </p>

  <h2>Confidentiality</h2>
  <p>
    We treat what you share with us for a session as confidential, use it only to prepare for and
    deliver the session, and do not disclose it except to people at RML who need it for that
    purpose, or where the law requires. Please tell us in advance if the material you intend to
    share is subject to restrictions, for example under a donor or government agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>Our advice and your decisions</h2>
  <p>
    Advisory sessions give you our professional opinion on the material you have provided. They are
    not legal, accounting, or investment advice, and they do not guarantee any result, approval, or
    funding outcome. Decisions made after a session are yours. To the fullest extent the law
    allows, RML's total liability arising from a session is limited to the fee you paid for it,
    and we are not liable for indirect or consequential loss. Nothing here limits liability that
    cannot lawfully be limited.
  </p>

  <h2>Ownership of the memo</h2>
  <p>
    You own the written memo once the fee is paid, and may use and share it within your
    organization and with your partners and funders. RML keeps ownership of its methods, templates,
    and pre-existing materials, and of any general know-how used to prepare the memo.
  </p>

  <h2>Personal data</h2>
  <p>
    We handle the personal data you give us when booking as described in our
    <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes and governing law</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms, but a change does not affect a session you have already paid for.
    These terms are governed by the laws of Jamaica, and the courts of Jamaica have jurisdiction
    over any dispute. Before either of us starts proceedings, we will first try in good faith to
    resolve the matter by discussion.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Bookings, invoices, and refunds: <strong
      ><a href="mailto:info@resultsmatrix.com">info@resultsmatrix.com</a></strong
    >.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
